`.\n\nThis item asks both.\n\nThe gate reads the commit. Each iteration's criteria, selected tests and tenant checks run in a detached worktree of `HEAD` (`gate_checkout`: `git worktree add --detach`, removed when the iteration's gate is done), never in the executor's directory. A file written and not committed cannot pass a criterion, a test or a check on the executor's behalf; a tenant checks command that writes beside itself writes into the worktree and is gone with it. The pre-executor probe (`[checks].probe`) still runs against the approved tree in place, as it did.\n\nAn empty iteration is told so. When an iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the gate runs (on the approved tree, where the criteria already fail), the log and the feedback both carry \"you committed nothing: no commit since <start>; N path(s) modified or untracked in the working tree, which the gate does not read\" and \"commit your work; the gate reads the commit, not the tree\", and the loop continues. An executor that answers `done` before committing on its first iteration and commits on its second passes as before (`test_an_empty_iteration_is_fed_back_and_a_later_commit_passes`).\n\nAn empty build is halted. A build is empty when the tree its record names is the approved tree outside `paths.records`: `git diff --quiet <approval sha> HEAD -- . ':!<records>'` finds nothing. The comparison is against the approval, not the attempt's own `start_sha`, so a retried attempt whose head already carries a prior attempt's valid commits adopts them and owes no commit of its own; an attempt that ends on the approved tree, whatever it left in the working directory, is what #227 was. When the last iteration ends empty, the record is `halted` with a new stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, detail \"the executor committed nothing; ...\" with the count of paths left in the tree; an earlier empty iteration is fed back and the loop continues. The class is the executor's, so counsel reads it and a steer retries it under R3; no new family. `STOP_CLASSES` and the build and verify schemas carry `empty` (build/9, verify/8). The status can never be `pass` on the approved tree.\n\nVerify refuses an empty build. A passing build record whose tree is the approved tree outside `paths.records` is refused before any adapter runs: \"the latest build record names no change; nothing to review\". The build no longer writes such a record; the refusal is verify's own guard against any record shaped this way, whoever wrote it.\n\nThe doctor's seventh proof: no attested item is empty. For every merged, fully-staged item, the passing build's tree differs from the approved tree outside `paths.records`. `[doctor].built_since` names a commit at or before which merges are before the window: named on every run, never failed, so #227 stands on the record as the specimen and the tenant is not red forever. Absent, the window is proof three's. A build record whose approval cannot be resolved is counted as not readable, not failed. This repository declares `built_since = \"dae6d765f3d6\"`, #227's merge. The proof's test is dogfood like the other five and is deselected from `[tests].run` and the CI test job the same way; the doctor job runs it.\n\nNot in this item: re-doing #227's change (its own item, filed on this product once merged); a ruling record voiding an attestation (R4); reading records from `HEAD` in every stage (R5); an executor-side change to the adapter (the instruction already says commit and stop; a mechanism is what was missing, not a sentence).\n\nThe stub under `stub/` is the change: `gate_checkout` and the empty-iteration handling in `attavo/build.py`, the class in `attavo/stops.py` and the two schemas, verify's refusal, proof seven and the manifest key, the fixture adapter's `ATTAVO_FIXTURE_NO_COMMIT`, the self-tenant's window and deselect, and seven tests red on the tree (v0.29.0). `tests/test_cli_help.py::test_help_names_the_seventh_proof_and_the_empty_stop` is red